From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:07:34 +0000
Subject: media: iris: Preserve timestamps on error buffers

Iris clears the timestamp when returning a buffer with
V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR, even if firmware supplied a valid timestamp.
With a corrupted HEVC frame on HFI gen2, firmware returns the frame
with HFI_INFO_DATA_CORRUPT and its original timestamp, but userspace
receives an empty error buffer with timestamp zero. This prevents
clients such as libva-v4l2 from identifying the failed picture and
can leave them waiting for it until a synchronization timeout.

Copy the recorded timestamp to error buffers so userspace can
associate the error with the corresponding input. Keep the error
state and zero payload unchanged; this does not assume that the
corrupted image is suitable for display.

Fixes: b791dcfcba3a ("media: iris: Add handling for corrupt and drop frames")
Signed-off-by: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
(cherry picked from commit 02a49632a858612e321a9136e3e9ef87c1af2257)
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c
@@ -902,7 +902,8 @@ int iris_vb2_buffer_done(struct iris_inst *inst, struct iris_buffer *buf)
 	if (buf->flags & V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR) {
 		state = VB2_BUF_STATE_ERROR;
 		vb2_set_plane_payload(vb2, 0, 0);
-		vb2->timestamp = 0;
+		/* Allow userspace to associate the error with the input frame. */
+		vb2->timestamp = buf->timestamp;
 		v4l2_m2m_buf_done(vbuf, state);
 		return 0;
 	}
